  "api_error_status": null,
  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for NRS_484B_127_2: 12 witnesses, 10 names, no composed rules. That took 2 of the 6 gate runs. The first run was wasted: I ran it on the untouched skeleton by mistake, so it returned `UNUSED_CLAIM` for every claim.\n\n**The rule** (`NRS_484B_127_2.lean`):\n- **Who it applies to:** a truck or combination of vehicles at least 80 inches wide. It does not apply on a road whose lane, occupied by the subject, has two or more lanes in its direction.\n- **The duty:** for every wide truck or combination directly ahead of the subject in its lane, with no other road user between them, one of these must hold:\n  - **Conditions don't permit:** the subject has not had that same leader, with neither vehicle stopped, for the full 30 s look-back window.\n  - **Overtaking:** within the next 10 s the subject overtakes and passes a vehicle or a combination of vehicles.\n  - **The space:** the gap along the road to the leader is at least 500 feet.\n- **Literals:** \"two\" is written as `Units.ratio 2 1` with a count unit, because there is no count constructor; the gate accepted it.\n- **Narrowings:** I added none.\n\n**The witnesses:** all 8 planned scenarios have their planned verdicts. I added four more so that every condition in the rule changes at least one witness's verdict:\n\n| Witness | Scene | Expected |\n|---|---|---|\n| `branch_5` | a combination of vehicles follows another combination at 60 m | violated |\n| `branch_6` | a car runs between the two trucks | compliant |\n| `branch_7` | the subject passes a bicycle on the shoulder, which does not count as overtaking a vehicle | violated |\n| `branch_8` | a car between the trucks pulled off 5 s ago | compliant |\n\nThe node has one oddity, which I didn't treat as a defect: in g5 the \"combination of vehicles\" class adds nothing, because the vehicle definition already includes trailers and combinations. I kept it because the node claims it, and the gate did not flag it.\n\nEarly on I tried a shell command that combined the gate with a directory listing; it needed approval and was denied, so I used the Read tool for Core files instead.\n\n`task_result.md` with the run log and these choices is in the working directory.",
